Ok, I think I understand--since you're seeing the outside of those walls,
they should be 'lit' only by the light on this side--and, since it's a dark
hallway, there isn't any light, and thus you shouldn't be able to see them
until you get close enough for your personal light source to show them.
Right?

Of course, this isn't a line of sight issue, since the walls are, indeed,
within your character's LOS.  Just because you haven't walked down the
passageway yet doesn't mean you can't see that far.  (I should note that I
play with lit_corridor, which does something very similar.)  It's more of a
lighting/visibility issue.  Not that this changes much, but it helps me
understand it better...



